From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: i2c: add the Samsung OIS MCU

Samsung's phone camera modules with optical image stabilisation have an
STM32G0 running Samsung's OIS firmware: it reads its own gyroscope and
moves the lens sideways, controlled over I2C. Describe its supplies,
NRST and BOOT0, the image sensor whose lens it stabilises, the gyro
polarity and orientation for the board (stock's pole-values and
gyro-orientation), and the module EEPROM's OIS calibration block, which
holds the factory gyro gains.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/samsung,ois-mcu-stm32g.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/samsung,ois-mcu-stm32g.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..278e698
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/samsung,ois-mcu-stm32g.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/media/i2c/samsung,ois-mcu-stm32g.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Samsung optical image stabilisation MCU (STM32G0)
+
+maintainers:
+  - Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
+
+description:
+  Samsung camera modules with optical image stabilisation have an STM32G0
+  microcontroller running Samsung's OIS firmware from its own flash. It
+  reads a gyroscope, drives the lens of one or more camera modules
+  sideways to cancel hand shake, and is controlled over I2C with 16-bit
+  big-endian register addresses. It stabilises the lens of the camera
+  sensor given in samsung,camera-sensor while that sensor is powered, and
+  takes the position of the sensor's focus lens (its lens-focus) to
+  compensate the shift of the optical centre with focus.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: samsung,ois-mcu-stm32g
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  vdig-supply:
+    description: MCU core supply
+
+  vaf-supply:
+    description: Lens driver supply, shared with the focus actuator
+
+  vio-supply:
+    description: I/O supply
+
+  reset-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: NRST of the MCU
+
+  boot0-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      BOOT0 of the MCU. Held low, so that the MCU runs its firmware rather
+      than the ROM bootloader.
+
+  samsung,camera-sensor:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      The image sensor whose lens this MCU stabilises. Stabilisation runs
+      while the sensor is powered.
+
+  samsung,gyro-polarity:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    description:
+      Polarity of the gyroscope's X and Y axes for this module, as mounted
+      on the board.
+    items:
+      - maximum: 0xff
+      - maximum: 0xff
+    default: [0, 0]
+
+  samsung,gyro-orientation:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    description: Orientation of the gyroscope on the board.
+    maximum: 0xff
+    default: 0
+
+  nvmem-cells:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      The OIS calibration block of the camera module's EEPROM, with the
+      factory gyro gains at offset 0x10 and their mark (0xbb when present)
+      at offset 0x30.
+
+  nvmem-cell-names:
+    const: calibration
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - vdig-supply
+  - vaf-supply
+  - vio-supply
+  - reset-gpios
+  - samsung,camera-sensor
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+
+    i2c {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
+
+        ois@62 {
+            compatible = "samsung,ois-mcu-stm32g";
+            reg = <0x62>;
+
+            vdig-supply = <&vreg_ois_vdig>;
+            vaf-supply = <&vreg_cam_vaf>;
+            vio-supply = <&vreg_ois_vio>;
+
+            reset-gpios = <&tlmm 173 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+            boot0-gpios = <&tlmm 168 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+
+            samsung,camera-sensor = <&cam_wide>;
+            samsung,gyro-polarity = <0 0>;
+            samsung,gyro-orientation = <0x10>;
+
+            nvmem-cells = <&wide_ois_cal>;
+            nvmem-cell-names = "calibration";
+        };
+    };
+...
